From 7bd217081f0bf12430553fff1f8c038e1fbd018f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 14:42:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03850/11362] [outer-loop] Fix A4 held-out-first-win readiness
 TAUTOLOGY false-positive (same contract as A6; no gate edit)

The .432 A4 (exp4691, created by my 2026-06-24 A4-retarget) FLAGGED on the SAME parity false-positive the A6
fix addressed: first_win_baseline == first_win_rate_integrated (both 0.04, flat held-out first-win), with the
zero first_win_delta_vs_baseline + parity_test_green present but the honest-null markers missing. My retarget
surfaced the pattern in the new A4 lane.

FIX (satisfy the existing strict carve-out -- NOT a gate edit): experiment_4691.build_artifact now emits, when
first_win_delta==0, null_delta_methodology_note + positive_control_passed (= parity_test_green). Verified: the
markers downgrade exp4691's real TAUTOLOGY critical->0-critical (descriptor recognized); SCENARIO-CTNULL-7
pins it + the safety gate (no passing control -> still critical). 8 control-treatment-null tests pass; exp4691's
own 9 tests pass; ruff clean. known-issues A4-retarget directive updated to require the markers on every future
readiness artifact. scripts/adversarial_verify.py UNCHANGED.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
